\\"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"  apps/"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},"<"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"nam"],["span",{"class":"sk-140thh"},"e"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},">"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"/"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},"<"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"nam"],["span",{"class":"sk-140thh"},"e"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},">"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},".bin"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"}," apps/"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},"<"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"nam"],["span",{"class":"sk-140thh"},"e"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},">"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"/demo.mp4"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"}," apps/"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},"<"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"nam"],["span",{"class":"sk-140thh"},"e"],["span",{"class":"sk-1itgoe"},">"],["span",{"class":"sk-mdbnqw"},"/demo.txt"],["span",{"class":"sk-140thh"}," [w] [h]"]]]],"\n",["p",0,"Steps: ",["code",0,"key <X11name>"],", ",["code",0,"chord <mods>+<key>"],", ",["code",0,"type <text>"],", ",["code",0,"move <x> <y>"],",\n",["code",0,"click [button]"],", ",["code",0,"wait <seconds>"],"."],"\n",["p",0,["strong",0,"This records on a private headless compositor, not on the user's desktop."],"\nIt starts its own ",["code",0,"sway"]," with its own Wayland socket, its own virtual output at\nthe size you ask for, and its own seat. That matters more than it sounds:"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,"Nothing appears on the user's screen, so a recording can never interrupt\nthem."],"\n",["li",0,"There is one window on that seat, so ",["code",0,"wtype"]," cannot type into somebody\nelse's app and no focus can be stolen mid-take."],"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"No lock, and no queue."]," Several of these run at once, which is the point."],"\n",["li",0,"The window is exactly the size you asked for rather than a tiling slot."],"\n"],"\n",["p",0,"The older ",["code",0,"record-app.sh"]," drives the user's live compositor and is kept only\nfor the rare case that needs the real session. Everything it went wrong at —\ncapturing another agent's window, keystrokes landing elsewhere, crash toasts in\nframe, and a shared lock that one orphaned process could hold for half an hour\n— came from sharing one seat, and none of it survives here."],"\n",["p",0,["strong",0,"Pointer steps do not work on this seat, and demos must be keyboard-driven."],"\nThe compositor runs with no input devices, so the seat never gains a pointer\ncapability and no client is ever sent motion or button. ",["code",0,"swaymsg seat cursor"],"\nreports success anyway — it moves sway's own cursor — which is why this looked\nlike it worked for a long time. ",["code",0,"wlrctl"]," speaks the right protocol but its move\nis relative and a click still reaches nobody. Verified by clicking a calculator\nkeypad and watching nothing happen. The recorder warns once if a steps file\nuses ",["code",0,"move"]," or ",["code",0,"click"],"."],"\n",["p",0,"Every application here is keyboard-usable, which is what makes that acceptable."],"\n",["p",0,"Always verify a take by extracting frames with\n",["code",0,"ffmpeg -ss <t> -i out.mp4 -frames:v 1 frame.png"]," and looking at them."],"\n",["p",0,["strong",0,"The whole take is driven through one ",["code",0,"wtype"]," process."]," Running it per step\ncycles the seat's keyboard capability for every keystroke, and a client's\nre-bind is asynchronous — it asks for a keyboard and the keymap and focus\narrive afterwards, so a key pressed in that window is gone. Two agents measured\nthe loss independently at roughly ",["strong",0,"one key in five"],", which is worse than it\nsounds: a dropped key does not merely omit a step, it redirects the ones after\nit, and one take left a mail demo deleting the wrong conversation. Batched,\nthree consecutive nine-step runs landed 27 of 27."],"\n",["p",0,["code",0,"wait"]," becomes wtype's own ",["code",0,"-s"],", so waits happen inside that single process.\nA step's text may not begin with ",["code",0,"-"],"; the recorder refuses rather than typing a\nflag into your application."],"\n",["p",0,"Each invocation is also led by a shift press and release. The first event of an\ninvocation is the one exposed to the re-bind window, and a bare ",["code",0,"key"]," step that\nloses it loses the ",["strong",0,"whole step"]," — where a ",["code",0,"type"]," step only loses its first\ncharacter. A modifier pressed and released produces nothing whether it arrives\nor not, so it is the right thing to sacrifice. With it, three runs of six bare\n",["code",0,"key"]," steps landed six of six each time."],"\n",["p",0,"A private compositor is also the way to drive an app interactively without a\nrecording — start one, point ",["code",0,"WAYLAND_DISPLAY"]," at it, and use ",["code",0,"grim"]," for\nstills."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"rules"},"Rules"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,"Own only your ",["code",0,"apps/<name>/"]," directory. Do not edit ",["code",0,"palmy/"],", ",["code",0,"shadcn/"],",\n",["code",0,"apps/kit/"],", ",["code",0,"parity/"]," or another app."],"\n",["li",0,"If palmy or shadcn is missing something you need, work around it in your app\nand ",["strong",0,"report the gap"]," — do not patch the toolkit."],"\n",["li",0,"Build to your own ",["code",0,"-out"]," path."],"\n",["li",0,"The package is not shared between apps, so you cannot break another agent's\nbuild. Take your time and get it right."],"\n"],"\n",["h2",{"id":"safety-when-the-app-touches-the-system"},"Safety when the app touches the system"],"\n",["p",0,["code",0,"network/"]," and ",["code",0,"bluetooth/"]," drive the real machine. Build the full\nfunctionality, but ",["strong",0,"when recording a demo do not disrupt the user's live\nconnection"],": do not disconnect the active wifi, do not forget a saved network,\ndo not unpair an existing device. Demonstrate scanning, listing, inspecting\ndetails, and at most toggling something you immediately restore. Say in your\nreport exactly which operations your demo performed."]]}